{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5c7a1e40-8f3b-4a2e-9d6c-3b1f6e2a9c10",
    "name": "LVS Streaming Platform API",
    "description": "Real-time live streaming & group voice chat platform backend.\n\nCovers auth, rooms, LiveKit token issuance, and LiveKit webhooks.\n\n## How to use\n1. Import this collection and set `baseUrl` (defaults to `http://localhost:5000`, matching `docker compose up`).\n2. Run **Auth > Register (Host)** and **Auth > Register (Guest)** first — their test scripts save `hostToken`/`hostUserId` and `guestToken`/`guestUserId` as collection variables automatically.\n3. Run **Rooms > Create Room (Host)** — its test script saves `roomId`.\n4. Everything downstream (join, leave, LiveKit token, webhook) reads those saved variables, so requests can be run in order without manual copy-pasting.\n\nAll responses share one envelope: `{ success, message, data }` on success, `{ success: false, code, message, errors? }` on failure — except `GET /health`, which is a plain `{ status, uptime }` for load balancers/Docker healthchecks, by design.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "guestToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "guestUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "roomId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] },
            "description": "Liveness probe used by Docker's HEALTHCHECK and any load balancer. Deliberately NOT wrapped in the `{success,message,data}` envelope — this is the one documented exception."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"has status:ok\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ok\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register (Host)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Host User\",\n  \"email\": \"host+{{$timestamp}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-battery\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates the user who will host the demo room. `profileImage` is optional (must be a URL if provided). Rate-limited (20 requests / 15 min, Redis-backed) alongside `/login`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"returns a token and no passwordHash\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.token).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.user).to.not.have.property(\"passwordHash\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hostToken\", body.data.token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hostUserId\", body.data.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register (Guest)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Guest User\",\n  \"email\": \"guest+{{$timestamp}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-battery\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a second user, used throughout the collection as the non-host participant (joins the room, receives socket-scoped events, is the subject of the LiveKit webhook example)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"guestToken\", body.data.token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"guestUserId\", body.data.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"host@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"correct-horse-battery\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Edit the email to match a user you've already registered (the Register requests above use a timestamped email, so this example won't match them out of the box — that's expected)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 or 401\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 401]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - wrong password (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"host@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"definitely-wrong\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Demonstrates the error envelope: `{success:false, code:\"INVALID_CREDENTIALS\", message}`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"401 with INVALID_CREDENTIALS\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"INVALID_CREDENTIALS\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get current user (me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "users", "me"] },
            "description": "Identity is re-loaded from MongoDB on every call (never trusted from JWT claims), so a deleted/changed user takes effect immediately rather than at token expiry."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"no passwordHash\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.not.have.property(\"passwordHash\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user - no token (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "users", "me"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test(\"401 Unauthorized\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rooms",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Room (Host)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Morning Show\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "rooms"] },
            "description": "The creator is auto-joined as host in the same request (via the room state service's `join()`), so `participantCount` is already 1 in the response — no separate join call needed for the host."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"host auto-joined\", () => pm.expect(body.data.participantCount).to.eql(1));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"roomId\", body.data.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Room - name too short (422)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"ab\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "rooms"] },
            "description": "Room names must be 3-80 characters (Zod boundary validation). Demonstrates `VALIDATION_ERROR` with a field-level `errors` map."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"422 VALIDATION_ERROR\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"VALIDATION_ERROR\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List Rooms",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
                { "key": "limit", "value": "20" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only `status: \"live\"` rooms, newest first. Returns `participantCount` per room via one pipelined Redis SCARD per room (not N sequential round trips) — deliberately does NOT return a full `participants` array here; that's reserved for the single-room detail endpoint."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"list items have no participants array\", () => {",
                  "  const rooms = pm.response.json().data.rooms;",
                  "  if (rooms.length > 0) pm.expect(rooms[0]).to.not.have.property(\"participants\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Room Detail",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "{{roomId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Unlike the list endpoint, this returns the full `participants: [{id, name}]` array — a single Redis SMEMBERS + one batched Mongo `find` for names, not N individual lookups."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK with participants array\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.participants).to.be.an(\"array\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Room Detail - not found (404)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "507f1f77bcf86cd799439011"]
            },
            "description": "A syntactically valid but non-existent ObjectId → `ROOM_NOT_FOUND`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"404 ROOM_NOT_FOUND\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"ROOM_NOT_FOUND\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Join Room (Guest)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{guestToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/join",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "{{roomId}}", "join"]
            },
            "description": "Idempotent — run this twice and the second call still returns 200 with the same participantCount, not an error and not a double-count."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"participantCount is now 2\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.participantCount).to.eql(2));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Join Room again (idempotent)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{guestToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/join",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "{{roomId}}", "join"]
            },
            "description": "Same guest, same room, second call — proves join() is idempotent (SADD on an existing member returns 0, no double-count, no error)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK, count unchanged\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.participantCount).to.eql(2);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.joined).to.eql(false);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Leave Room (Guest)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{guestToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/leave",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "{{roomId}}", "leave"]
            },
            "description": "A non-host leaving does NOT end the room. Also idempotent — safe to call again."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK, room not ended\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.roomEnded).to.eql(false);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Leave Room (Host) - ends the room",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/leave",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "{{roomId}}", "leave"]
            },
            "description": "Run this LAST in the Rooms folder — the host leaving transitions the room to `ended` (terminal state). Room membership for anyone still inside converges at this point too."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK, host leaving ends the room\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.roomEnded).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Join Room - ended room (409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{guestToken}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/join",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rooms", "{{roomId}}", "join"]
            },
            "description": "Run this AFTER \"Leave Room (Host) - ends the room\" above, against the same {{roomId}}. Joining an ended room is rejected; leaving one is not (leave stays idempotent so nobody gets stranded)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"409 ROOM_ENDED\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"ROOM_ENDED\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "LiveKit",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Token (Host)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{hostUserId}}\",\n  \"roomName\": \"{{roomId}}\",\n  \"role\": \"host\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/livekit/token", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "livekit", "token"] },
            "description": "`userId` in the body must match the caller's own verified JWT identity — it's checked, never trusted (see the next request for what happens when it doesn't match). `role` in the body is accepted for shape-compatibility with the brief's documented example but is NEVER what determines the grant: the server derives host-vs-participant solely from `room.host`. The returned token is a real, usable LiveKit JWT — paste it into `serverUrl` + `token` in LiveKit's Meet sample or your own client to actually connect."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK with a token\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.token).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.roomName).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"roomId\"));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Token (Guest, participant)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{guestToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{guestUserId}}\",\n  \"roomName\": \"{{roomId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/livekit/token", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "livekit", "token"] },
            "description": "The guest is not `room.host`, so the derived grant is participant-level (audio publish + subscribe, no `roomAdmin`) regardless of any `role` sent in the body."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Token - identity mismatch (403)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{guestToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{hostUserId}}\",\n  \"roomName\": \"{{roomId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/livekit/token", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "livekit", "token"] },
            "description": "The guest's own JWT is used for auth, but the body claims the HOST's userId. This is the identity-spoofing guard: rejected before any room lookup or LiveKit call happens, specifically so a caller can't probe room existence via someone else's identity."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"403 IDENTITY_MISMATCH\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"IDENTITY_MISMATCH\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Token - room not found (404)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{hostUserId}}\",\n  \"roomName\": \"507f1f77bcf86cd799439011\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/livekit/token", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "livekit", "token"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test(\"404 ROOM_NOT_FOUND\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Webhook - participant_left (signed example)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "{{webhookSignature}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{{webhookBody}}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/livekit/webhook",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "livekit", "webhook"]
            },
            "description": "LiveKit itself calls this — not a client — but this request builds and sends a genuinely-signed test payload so the endpoint can be demonstrated standalone.\n\n**Requires `livekitApiKey`/`livekitApiSecret` collection variables** set to the same values as `backend/.env`'s `LIVEKIT_API_KEY`/`LIVEKIT_API_SECRET` (Postman's pre-request script signs the body the same way LiveKit's real servers do: an HS256 JWT over the body's SHA-256 hash, issued by the API key).\n\nRun this once, then run it again unchanged — the second delivery is dropped by the dedupe guard (same event id, claimed already) rather than reconciled twice. Change the `id` field in the pre-request script to get a fresh, non-deduped event."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const apiKey = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"livekitApiKey\");",
                  "const apiSecret = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"livekitApiSecret\");",
                  "",
                  "if (!apiKey || !apiSecret) {",
                  "  console.warn(\"Set collection variables livekitApiKey / livekitApiSecret (same as backend/.env) to sign this webhook.\");",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "const roomId = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"roomId\") || \"000000000000000000000000\";",
                  "const guestUserId = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"guestUserId\") || \"000000000000000000000001\";",
                  "",
                  "const body = JSON.stringify({",
                  "  event: \"participant_left\",",
                  "  id: \"postman-evt-\" + Date.now(),",
                  "  createdAt: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000),",
                  "  room: { name: roomId },",
                  "  participant: { identity: guestUserId }",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "function base64url(wordArray) {",
                  "  return CryptoJS.enc.Base64.stringify(wordArray)",
                  "    .replace(/\\+/g, \"-\").replace(/\\//g, \"_\").replace(/=+$/, \"\");",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "const header = { alg: \"HS256\", typ: \"JWT\" };",
                  "const nowSec = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
                  "const payload = {",
                  "  iss: apiKey,",
                  "  sha256: CryptoJS.SHA256(body).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Base64),",
                  "  iat: nowSec,",
                  "  exp: nowSec + 300",
                  "};",
                  "",
                  "const headerB64 = base64url(CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify(header)));",
                  "const payloadB64 = base64url(CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify(payload)));",
                  "const signingInput = headerB64 + \".\" + payloadB64;",
                  "const signature = base64url(CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(signingInput, apiSecret || \"placeholder\"));",
                  "const jwt = signingInput + \".\" + signature;",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"webhookBody\", body);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"webhookSignature\", jwt);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK (processed or already-processed)\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Webhook - bad signature (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "not-a-valid-signature" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event\": \"participant_left\",\n  \"id\": \"evt-bad-sig\",\n  \"room\": { \"name\": \"{{roomId}}\" },\n  \"participant\": { \"identity\": \"{{guestUserId}}\" }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/livekit/webhook",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "livekit", "webhook"]
            },
            "description": "No valid JWT signature — rejected before any reconciliation logic runs."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": ["pm.test(\"401 Unauthorized\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
